      "writtenOn": "2021-09-30T09:38:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, not for bundle. \n\nSome vulnerabilities exploit the fact that there are quite a few parcelables that use the untyped read/write container APIs (https://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/Parcel#untyped-containers) and that those APIs trigger deserialization regardless of the type expected [1] [2]. Our goal is to move developers to the APIs you mentioned readTypedXXX() / writeTypedXXX() since they are also more performant and that will be our 1st recommendation indeed. If most parcelables respected http://go/android-api-guidelines#parcelable-final, this would be sufficient. However, a quick code-search tells us that our codebase from ~4k parcelables in our codebase (https://source.corp.google.com/search?q\u003dclass.*implements%5CsParcelable\u0026sq\u003dpackage:%5Eandroid$), only around ~1.5k are final (https://source.corp.google.com/search?q\u003dclass.*implements%5CsParcelable\u0026sq\u003dpackage:%5Eandroid$), one such example we\u0027ve hit is here (https://googleplex-android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/frameworks/base/+/15778315/3..5/core/java/android/content/pm/InstantAppIntentFilter.java#b62), so we also want to provide a way to migrate to safe deserialization of these types too, especially the ones where the work to ensure final classes is realistically not get done. So, in summary, the plan is to point developers away from untyped APIs to the ones you mentioned readTypedXXX() / writeTypedXXX() and to migrate (and ask owners to migrate) inside the platform, but for the cases where this isn\u0027t possible we are going to migrate to the ones being introduced here. \n\n[1] You can see in https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/12XbcaOJzi2aD27efKy4XDZ3OM44U3Q812rykUFVbhOo/edit#slide\u003did.gdf637bd3fe_1_193 that the attacker use the fact that OutputConfiguration was using Parcel.readList() to insert a certain vulnerable parcelable responsible for part of the exploit chain.\n[2] This is also summarized in http://go/safer-parcel#heading\u003dh.emkgx0ugb6hh.",
