      "writtenOn": "2021-09-29T16:54:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "question from the longer comment, in other words, if \u0027T\u0027 is Integer here, what would we expect to be passed for Class?\n\n- Integer.class \u003d\u003e we\u0027ll get ClassCastException (different than BadParcelableException for the parcelable case, but because of b/150808347, specifically getExceptionCode returns success for this exception type, as far as I can tell, the exception would be silently dropped from clients). We should prefer to have the same exception types, and we should only throw exception types that won\u0027t be dropped.\n- null \u003d\u003e it would be allowed to read any parcelable type",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3373,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 3373,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "2970e3a5dd56dd6a10f61f66b853c4de1698c2b6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f850aea3_cf25fe09",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/Parcel.java",
