      },
      "lineNbr": 3373,
      "author": {
        "id": 1133744
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-29T17:38:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought about this, but I\u0027m not sure the bug you linked should guide what we throw here. That seems like a problem that should be separately addressed (or not and it\u0027s WAI) and we throw what semantically makes sense here, after all we\u0027re not necessarily always in a binder thread and there are probably other places that throw CCE too.\n\nThinking about the semantics: BadParcelableException will be thrown if the object on the wire is a parcelable and this agrees with the javadoc (\"Exception thrown when a **Parcelable** is malformed or otherwise invalid\"). For non-parcelable cases I\u0027m not sure BadParcelableException makes sense since it doesn\u0027t involve parcelables and ClassCastException is the natural choice in Java. For example, this is what would happen if you tried to use old API and cast to int:\n\n  int integer \u003d (int) p.readValue(null);\n\nThis throws CCE. I think we should stick to this behavior?",
      "parentUuid": "4089dd86_409e8d91",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3373,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 3373,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "2970e3a5dd56dd6a10f61f66b853c4de1698c2b6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b79dd2d0_14e1e9b3",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/Parcel.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 3373,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-29T18:15:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I\u0027m not sure the bug you linked should guide what we throw here\n\nI think this is Parcel#getExceptionCode. Though, maybe we should have a test of this case in any case?\n\nIt\u0027s not really possible to fix that bug or change the semantics of how errors are thrown here, because the behavior is essentially frozen in the API and 1,000s of call sites. We need to choose pragmatic errors. ClassCastException is incidental here, and it is related to the fact that we parse the parcel, and then we try to cast the class. If we detected the mismatch earlier (and we do have the information to do this), then there would be no class to cast incorrectly. Either way, the parcelable is malformed.\n\nBtw - does that mean implicitly that if we want to read Integer, we should pass Integer.class?",
      "parentUuid": "f850aea3_cf25fe09",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3373,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 3373,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "2970e3a5dd56dd6a10f61f66b853c4de1698c2b6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "57ab2c63_4954b6f9",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/Parcel.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 3373,
      "author": {
        "id": 1133744
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-30T09:38:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We wouldn\u0027t change the semantics of the current errors thrown here as the CCE would only be thrown in new APIs (which incorporate the example I mentioned earlier into the class), but ack if the semantics around this class revolve around BPE. I\u0027m not strongly opposed to your suggestion and since you\u0027re the expert, let\u0027s change to BPE :) \n\nIf you want to read an Integer you can:\n\n1. Use the old API and cast yourself (if fail CCE will be thrown)\n  int x \u003d (int) p.readValue(null);\n\n2. Use the new API and a BPE will be thrown (as agreed above) \n  int x \u003d p.readValue(null, Integer.class);",
      "parentUuid": "b79dd2d0_14e1e9b3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3373,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 3373,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "2970e3a5dd56dd6a10f61f66b853c4de1698c2b6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4636a856_6cfe1f9f",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/Parcel.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 3373,
      "author": {
        "id": 1133744
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-30T10:08:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ops, sorry, we\u0027re not actually introducing a new readValue() API, this is just internal for use by the actual APIs (readList() and readParcelable() here). So, if we\u0027re reading an integer list we could:\n\n  1: List\u003cInteger\u003e ints \u003d ...\n  2: p.readList(ints, null, Integer.class); // New API\n  3: p.readList(ints, null);                // Old API\n  4: int x \u003d ints.get(0);\n  \nIf the list on the payload is not of integers, a CCE will be thrown on L4 if using the old API, otherwise a BPE will be thrown on L2 using the new API.",
      "parentUuid": "57ab2c63_4954b6f9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3373,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 3373,
        "endChar": 27
